s; language processing across diverse populations; neural research methods used in language studies; applications of generative AI and large language models in modeling human language processes; and the use of AI and immersive technologies to enhance language learning. Students will gain an integrated understanding of how psychology, neuroscience, and artificial intelligence intersect to advance both research and educational practices in language. This course will meet with LING 591 LBT and PSYC 593 LBT."},{"crn":"62820","code":"QWR","typeCode":"ONL","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Online","typeCode":"ONL","days":["W"],"start":720,"end":1010,"location":"n.a.","instructors":["Goodnight, M"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"Meets with CI 552 A."},{"crn":"40618","code":"SPA","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["W"],"start":840,"end":1010,"location":"385 Education Building","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.","Restricted to MS:MentalHealthCounseling-UIUC."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":"Instructor Approval Required","sectionText":"Title: Survey of Psychological Assessment Methods. This course will meet in DRES Conference Room (107)."},{"crn":"34336","code":"TH","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["R"],"start":750,"end":920,"location":"108 David Kinley Hall","instructors":["Beard, J"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":"Instructor Approval Required","sectionText":"This course is designed to prepare you to work with individuals attempting to recover from addictions. It will c